<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Makarios III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1913">1913</a>–<a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Archbishop Makarios</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Makarios III was archbishop of the Church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> from 1950 and the first president of the Republic of Cyprus from 1960 until his death in 1977. Leader of the Greek Cypriot campaign for union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, he was exiled by the British to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seychelles">Seychelles</a> in 1956–1957. As president he faced intercommunal conflict, and a Greek-backed coup against him in 1974 led to the Turkish invasion of the island.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/makarios-iii.jpg" alt="Makarios III" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: New York World-Telegram and the Sun staff photographer: Fernandez, Orlando, photographer. Cropped by Badseed using The GIMP. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Makarios_III_and_Robert_F._Wagner_NYWTS_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
